      "message": "\u003e What does closing the RepoView improperly mean?\n\nWell, we should ask Dave 😊\n\n\u003e Does that contradict your fix?\n\nI do see the reference counting going up because of `repo \u003d repoManager.openRepository(project)` at L54. If the repo is opened, it *must* be closed; otherwise, the cache will increment its counter indefinitely.\n\n\u003e Shouldn\u0027t RepoView implement AutoClosable to ensure that it\u0027s always closed?\n\nYep, that\u0027s exactly what I thought, but if you see the constructor, it throws an exception, and that\u0027s what was blocking Dave from doing it:\n\n`RepoView(GitRepositoryManager repoManager, Project.NameKey project) throws IOException`",
